#{[17592186535075 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535075 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535075 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535075 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{z}\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ is defined by $z=y-3x$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $3x\\le y\\le 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535075 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e16a799c-84bb-5d3d-b669-6d70bdf08db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535075 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-3x)=-3,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-3x)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be evaluated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\sqrt{z}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{y-3x}\\sqrt{1+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{y-3x}\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}{∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{y-3x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{3x}^{3}\\sqrt{y-3x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}(y-3x)^{3/2}]}_{y=3x}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-3x)^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{3}\\,{[\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})(3-3x)^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{11}}{45}(0-{3}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{11}}{45}(9\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{33}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545192 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186545934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545192 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 175